\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf2 \strokec2 \
Autonomic markers fail to capture localized muscular microtrauma, stimulus-induced excitation-contraction coupling failure, or joint-specific inflammation. An athlete may register suppressed nocturnal SDNN due to psychological stress or late-evening thermal strain while retaining baseline force production in isolated movement patterns. Conversely, systemic parasympathetic saturation can co-occur with severe localized quadriceps damage following eccentric loading.\
Therefore, morning ARC score is treated as a systemic fatigue prior. It gates total daily volume and systemic cardiovascular/axial strain, but it cannot override mechanical tension requirements or cause continuous volume drops below MEV without secondary subjective validation.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa160\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs28 \cf2 Multi-Metric Priority Cascade\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs24 \cf2 To prevent noisy HRV signals from corrupting training prescriptions, daily gating follows an explicit hierarchically ordered cascade:\
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\partightenfactor0
\ls1\ilvl0
\f0\b \cf2 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	1	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Safety Red-Flags (Priority 1):
\f1\b0  User-reported sharp joint pain ($>4/10$), illness, or acute injury. Triggers immediate movement substitution or rest day recommendation.\
\ls1\ilvl0
\f0\b \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	2	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Subjective Recovery Composite (Priority 2):
\f1\b0  User-reported Perceived Soreness, Sleep Quality, and Stress (rated 1 to 5).\
\ls1\ilvl0
\f0\b \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	3	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 ARC Readiness Score (Priority 3):
\f1\b0  Morning SDNN relative to an individual 30-day rolling baseline $z$-score ($z_\{\\text\{ARC\}\}$).\
\ls1\ilvl0
\f0\b \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	4	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Prior-Day EWMA Acute Load Residual (Priority 4):
\f1\b0  Quantified fatigue residual calculated via systemic exponentially weighted workload tracking.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa160\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs28 \cf2 \strokec2 Readiness Band Definitions and Engine Actions\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs24 \cf2 The $z$-score for the morning ARC signal is calculated as:\
$$z_\{\\text\{ARC\}\} = \\frac\{\\text\{SDNN\}_\{\\text\{today\}\} - \\mu_\{\\text\{SDNN\}, 30d\}\}\{\\sigma_\{\\text\{SDNN\}, 30d\}\}$$\
Combined readiness scores merge subjective inputs ($S_\{\\text\{sub\}\}$, normalized $0.0 - 1.0$) with $z_\{\\text\{ARC\}\}$ to map athletes into four operational bands:\
$$\\text\{Readiness Index (RI)\} = 0.6 \\cdot \\left( \\frac\{z_\{\\text\{ARC\}\} + 3\}\{6\} \\right) + 0.4 \\cdot S_\{\\text\{sub\}\}$$\
$$\\text\{Readiness Index (RI)\} = 0.6 \\cdot \\left( \\frac\{z_\{\\text\{ARC\}\} + 3\}\{6\} \\right) + 0.4 \\cdot S_\{\\text\{sub\}\}$$\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa160\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs36 \cf2 Same-Day Gating Precedence Algorithm\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa160\partightenfactor0

\fs28 \cf2 High-Readiness Prescription Rule\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs24 \cf2 When an athlete enters a High/Peaking readiness state, the deterministic engine 
\f0\b must not add set volume
\f1\b0  beyond the planned mesocycle progression. Hypertrophic adaptation is driven by progressive mechanical overload within structured volume windows, not by reactive volume spikes that generate excess residual fatigue. High readiness permits intensity auto-selection (achieving higher absolute working loads for the target RPE/RIR window), but hard-set counts remain pinned to the mesocycle plan.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa160\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs28 \cf2 Protection of Weekly MEV Adherence\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs24 \cf2 Chronic low readiness risks stranding an athlete below MEV for consecutive weeks, leading to detraining or under-dosing. The engine protects MEV through a dynamic Volume Deficit Ledger (VDL):\
$$\\text\{VDL\}_\{\\text\{muscle\}\} = \\sum_\{d=1\}^\{t\} \\left( \\text\{Sets\}_\{\\text\{planned\}, d\} - \\text\{Sets\}_\{\\text\{executed\}, d\} \\right)$$\
If $\\text\{VDL\}_\{\\text\{muscle\}\}$ threatens to drop weekly completed volume below $\\text\{MEV\}_\{\\text\{muscle\}\}$ by day 5 of the microcycle:\
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\partightenfactor0
\ls2\ilvl0\cf2 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	1	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 The engine suspends set-trimming on compounds, enforcing an RPE cap of $7.5$ instead of trimming sets.\
\ls2\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	2	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 If low readiness persists for $>72$ consecutive hours despite RPE caps, the engine overrides daily session execution and converts the remaining microcycle into a Reactive Micro-Deload, resetting weekly volume requirements.\
