\f0\b\fs28 \cf2 \strokec2 Ordered Precedence Execution Algorithm for Low-Readiness Days\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs24 \cf2 When $\\text\{RI\} < 0.45$, the engine processes session modifications through an ordered, deterministic sequence. Processing halts immediately once the daily target set reduction factor ($M_V$) is satisfied.\
The engine executes modifications in the following order:\
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\partightenfactor0
\ls3\ilvl0
\f0\b \cf2 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Step 1: Apply RPE Ceiling.
\f1\b0  Clamp all prescribed RPE targets to $RPE_\{\\max\}$ ($7.0$ for Depleted, $8.0$ for Low). Absolute working load is recalculated based on the reduced RPE.\
\ls3\ilvl0
\f0\b \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Step 2: Trim Accessory Sets.
\f1\b0  Reduce sets from isolation and secondary machine slots (Slot Priority 3 and 4) by 1 set per slot until the daily set target ($M_V \\cdot \\text\{Sets\}_\{\\text\{prescribed\}\}$) is reached. If the target set reduction is satisfied, halt processing.\
\ls3\ilvl0
\f0\b \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Step 3: Equipment Swap (Axial-Fatigue Mitigation).
\f1\b0  If $\\text\{RI\} < 0.35$, replace high axial-load compounds (e.g., Barbell Squat, Romanian Deadlift) with low axial-load equivalents (e.g., Hack Squat, Lying Leg Curl). Exercise selection maps retain primary target muscle groups without altering the muscle ledger.\
\ls3\ilvl0
\f0\b \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Step 4: Trim Compound Sets.
\f1\b0  If set targets are not met after Step 2, trim 1 set from primary multi-joint compound slots (Slot Priority 1 and 2), provided the remaining daily sets for the target muscle remain $\\ge \\text\{MEV\}_\{\\text\{daily\\_floor\}\}$. If the target set reduction is satisfied, halt processing.\
\ls3\ilvl0
\f0\b \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Step 5: Convert Session to Technique/Pump.
\f1\b0  If $\\text\{RI\} < 0.30$ and set trimming would violate $\\text\{MEV\}_\{\\text\{daily\\_floor\}\}$, convert all remaining working sets to fixed RPE $\\le 6.0$ velocity/pump sets. Progression velocity tracking is disabled for the session.\
\ls3\ilvl0
\f0\b \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Step 6: Enforce Full Rest Day (Stop Condition).
\f1\b0  If $z_\{\\text\{ARC\}\} < -2.0$ AND Subjective Soreness $\\le 1.5/5$, OR if Step 5 fails to mitigate recovery deficits, the session status transitions to 
\fs30 \cf5 \cb6 \strokec5 CANCELLED_REST_RECOMMENDED
\fs24 \cf2 \cb1 \strokec2 . The engine shifts the remaining calendar according to the Drift Policy.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa160\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs28 \cf2 \strokec2 Intra-Session Autoregulation Rules\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs24 \cf2 Intra-session adjustments respond to acute failure or velocity loss during session execution:\
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\partightenfactor0
\ls4\ilvl0
\f0\b \cf2 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 RIR/RPE Miss (Over-shooting):
\f1\b0  If an athlete reaches absolute failure (RPE 10) on a set prescribed at RPE 8, the engine dynamically recalculates working load for subsequent sets of that exercise using a $-5\\%$ load reduction. If a second consecutive set misses the target RPE by $\\ge 1.5$ units, remaining sets for that exercise slot are dropped.\
\ls4\ilvl0
\f0\b \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Intra-Session Fatigue Drop-off:
\f1\b0  If RPE rises by $>2.0$ units across consecutive sets at identical loads, or if completed reps drop by $>30\\%$ between sets at equal load, the engine terminates the current exercise slot and cancels remaining secondary accessory slots for that target muscle.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa160\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs36 \cf2 \strokec2 Drift and Missed-Session Policy Matrix\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs24 \cf2 Schedule disruptions (drift) occur when sessions are executed late, out of order, partially logged, or skipped. The Helm deterministic engine resolves calendar drift using strict precedence rules to preserve Push-Pull-Legs (PPL) rotation integrity, prevent back-to-back exposure of identical muscle groups, and prevent acute workload spikes.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa160\partightenfactor0

