\f0\b\fs28 \cf2 \strokec2 Muscle Spacing Clamps\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs24 \cf2 To prevent structural overuse injuries and localized recovery failure, the engine enforces strict intra-muscle rest clamps. Primary multi-joint compound exercises require a minimum of 48 hours of elapsed recovery time between identical target muscle exposures, whereas secondary isolation accessories require a minimum of 24 hours.\
If a calendar shift causes a Pull session (targeting Latissimus Dorsi) to fall within 24 hours of a preceding Pull or Secondary Back exposure, the engine automatically transforms the schedule by swapping the sequence order or inserting an engine-enforced rest day:\
$$\\text\{Session Sequence\}_\{\\text\{adjusted\}\} = \\text\{Transform\}\\left( [\\text\{Pull\}, \\text\{Push\}] \\to [\\text\{Push\}, \\text\{Pull\}] \\right) \\quad \\text\{if \} \\Delta t_\{\\text\{Pull-Pull\}\} < 48\\text\{h\}$$\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa160\partightenfactor0

