\f0\b\fs36 \cf2 \cb1 \strokec2 Deload Policy: Scheduled and Reactive Frameworks\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs24 \cf2 Deloads facilitate structural tissue healing, systemic fatigue clearance, and central nervous system recovery while resensitizing skeletal muscle to hypertrophic stimuli. The Helm periodization engine governs both scheduled mesocycle deloads and reactive, condition-triggered micro-deloads.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa160\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs28 \cf2 Scheduled Deload Triggers and Execution\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs24 \cf2 Scheduled deloads occur at fixed mesocycle boundaries determined by athlete training age and baseline volume tolerance. Novice and intermediate athletes undergo a deload every 6th week (5 weeks of progressive overload followed by 1 week of deloading). Advanced athletes deload every 4th week (3 weeks of progressive overload followed by 1 week of deloading).\
During a scheduled deload, daily training parameters are constrained according to explicit numeric clamps:\
$$\\text\{Sets\}_\{\\text\{deload\}\} = \\max\\left( \\text\{MEV\}_\{\\text\{muscle\}\}, \\, \\text\{Round\}\\left( 0.50 \\cdot \\text\{Sets\}_\{\\text\{peak\\_week\}\} \\right) \\right)$$\
$$\\text\{Sets\}_\{\\text\{deload\}\} = \\max\\left( \\text\{MEV\}_\{\\text\{muscle\}\}, \\, \\text\{Round\}\\left( 0.50 \\cdot \\text\{Sets\}_\{\\text\{peak\\_week\}\} \\right) \\right)$$\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa160\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs28 \cf2 Reactive Deload Triggers\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs24 \cf2 A reactive deload overrides scheduled mesocycle timing when acute systemic fatigue threatens structural overload or overtraining syndrome. The engine evaluates reactive triggers daily using a binary decision structure evaluating three primary markers:\
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\partightenfactor0
\ls5\ilvl0
\f0\b \cf2 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	1	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Autonomic Suppression Trigger:
\f1\b0  Three or more consecutive training sessions categorized in the Depleted readiness band ($z_\{\\text\{ARC\}\} < -1.5$).\
\ls5\ilvl0
\f0\b \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	2	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Performance Regression Trigger:
\f1\b0  Two or more consecutive microcycles displaying a statistically significant drop in estimated 1RM ($\\text\{e1RM\}$) on primary compound movements despite reported RPE $\\ge 9.0$:\uc0\u8232 $$\\text\{e1RM\} = \\text\{Load\} \\cdot \\left(1 + \\frac\{\\text\{Reps\}\}\{30\}\\right)$$\u8232 \u8232 $$\\text\{Trigger Condition: \} \\frac\{\\text\{e1RM\}_\{\\text\{current\}\} - \\text\{e1RM\}_\{\\text\{baseline\}\}\}\{\\text\{e1RM\}_\{\\text\{baseline\}\}\} \\le -0.035$$\u8232 \
\ls5\ilvl0
\f0\b \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	3	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Joint Discomfort Trigger:
\f1\b0  Subjective joint soreness rating $\\ge 4.0 / 5.0$ persisting for four or more consecutive days across movement patterns sharing a joint axis.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa160\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs28 \cf2 \strokec2 Decision Protocol for Deload Severity\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs24 \cf2 The engine determines deload severity based on signal duration and physiological metrics:\
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\partightenfactor0
\ls6\ilvl0
\f0\b \cf2 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Single Easy Day:
\f1\b0  Triggered when ARC registers as Depleted for a single day while subjective soreness remains low ($<2.0$). Volume is cut by $50\\%$ for that single session, and RPE is capped at $\\le 6.0$.\
\ls6\ilvl0
\f0\b \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Full Reactive Deload Week:
\f1\b0  Triggered when ARC remains Depleted for three or more consecutive days, or when performance regression meets the threshold ($\\ge 3.5\\%$ drop in e1RM). Volume across the entire microcycle is reduced by $50\\%$ and RPE is capped at $\\le 5.0$.\
\ls6\ilvl0
\f0\b \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Regional Deload:
\f1\b0  Triggered when joint discomfort reaches $\\ge 4.0$ for four or more days. The engine reduces volume on affected joint movement patterns while maintaining normal training parameters for unaffected muscle groups.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa160\partightenfactor0

